{"id":"known:49e238fc4f12877401cf06640e790d7e","url":"/archive/known/?id=49e238fc4f12877401cf06640e790d7e","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"@ChrisAldrich It is also, I think, about making machine learning more accessible to teachers and academics long term. So in my syllabus for example I ","summary":"@ChrisAldrich It is also, I think, about making machine learning more accessible to teachers and academics long term. So in my syllabus for example I have objectives: http://edu307syllabus.networkedlearningcollaborative.com/ what if the meta data that I build into those could be connected to tags I put on replies to students? I could see these being used in ","date":"2018-04-19","published":"2018-04-19T17:54:10+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"http://quickthoughts.jgregorymcverry.com/2018/04/19/chrisaldrich-yeah-i-am-at-a-purely-philosophical-use-case","tags":[],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:5685ded1d643956999186d547c5adc84","url":"/archive/known/?id=5685ded1d643956999186d547c5adc84","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"@ChrisAldrich Yeah I am at a purely philosophical use case thinkery stage right now. There are tools that repositories use that import data. They must","summary":"@ChrisAldrich Yeah I am at a purely philosophical use case thinkery stage right now. There are tools that repositories use that import data. They must be assigning metadata to fields. I am thinking strictly in terms of @altmetric stuff for now and also thinking about building interlocked communities of open scholars in the future. Is this a use case? Or too ","date":"2018-04-19","published":"2018-04-19T17:47:38+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/ChrisAldrich/status/987023598291423232","tags":[],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:97aefa6b57b4059d9325de219dc9d6a9","url":"/archive/known/?id=97aefa6b57b4059d9325de219dc9d6a9","source":"known","type":"notes","title":"This is what I am exploring. For academics in our spaces whose #GoOpen, #oer, #digped, #DOO, philosophies align with #indieweb principles would the to","summary":"This is what I am exploring. For academics in our spaces whose #GoOpen, #oer, #digped, #DOO, philosophies align with #indieweb principles would the tools like MicroPub and MicroSub and standards like webmentions not only make tracking the spread of our stuff, but more importantly encouraging the spread and spirit, without recreating another silo. Regardless ","date":"2018-04-19","published":"2018-04-19T17:44:20+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"tags":["DOO","GoOpen","digped","indieweb","oer"],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:56802dd0a0f743055a725b96eb52cecb","url":"/archive/known/?id=56802dd0a0f743055a725b96eb52cecb","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"This is what I meant when I was discussing memes and images on the #indieweb chat yesterday. We need pathways on to the web for creatives. Read every ","summary":"This is what I meant when I was discussing memes and images on the #indieweb chat yesterday. We need pathways on to the web for creatives. Read every report about youth (US centric atleast). They want to to be the next Instagram and YouTube star not the next blogger. I remember talking to @toolness when he first launched x-ray goggles about what a remixable ","date":"2018-04-19","published":"2018-04-19T17:29:11+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://medium.com/twill/rethinking-the-creative-web-part-3-towards-a-new-read-write-web-185fe258690b","tags":["indieweb"],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
