{"id":"known:5aedd0c126195b57ed39ff0f15a84634","url":"/archive/known/?id=5aedd0c126195b57ed39ff0f15a84634","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"@cathieleblanc YI agree you are dead on. One cool thing, I am not just publishing on Twitter. I am publishing on my own site and using #indieweb power","summary":"@cathieleblanc YI agree you are dead on. One cool thing, I am not just publishing on Twitter. I am publishing on my own site and using #indieweb powered tools to syndicate this post to Twitter. Get the critical mass problem...but we are the masses","date":"2018-04-19","published":"2018-04-19T16:06:52+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/cathieleblanc/status/986999052486217729","tags":["indieweb"],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:4157b8128324c039dc38d3f8609555c1","url":"/archive/known/?id=4157b8128324c039dc38d3f8609555c1","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"@ottonomy Yes that is my ultimate goal. I asked around at #oer18 it looks like a group met around 2013 and wrote some standards around metadata. Looke","summary":"@ottonomy Yes that is my ultimate goal. I asked around at #oer18 it looks like a group met around 2013 and wrote some standards around metadata. Looked at @moodle metadata standards as well. I have my repos up now, but not publishing to gh-pages yet. Maybe I should. My ultimate goal is to have one file for each module and not have to update my syllabus and c","date":"2018-04-19","published":"2018-04-19T16:04:38+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/ottonomy/status/986992609867382784","tags":["oer18"],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:116a6e144ce8a82ebd0819c698536603","url":"/archive/known/?id=116a6e144ce8a82ebd0819c698536603","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"@ottonomy Hey Nate. Maybe you can point me in right direction. Rebuilding all my course repos but wondering about how others are thinking about metada","summary":"@ottonomy Hey Nate. Maybe you can point me in right direction. Rebuilding all my course repos but wondering about how others are thinking about metadata. I am trying to stay as plain html as possible but want to be forward thinking in tracking how material gets shared and remixed and making sure I have community building blocks set up.","date":"2018-04-19","published":"2018-04-19T15:29:27+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/986935130852741123","tags":[],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
