{"id":"known:91cb661f404943fbcc83b947a6609084","url":"/archive/known/?id=91cb661f404943fbcc83b947a6609084","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"@petermolnar That is my thinking. I am starting a HWC with my local chamber of commerce to focus on \"facebook only\" local businesses and going to spin","summary":"@petermolnar That is my thinking. I am starting a HWC with my local chamber of commerce to focus on \"facebook only\" local businesses and going to spin one up with out Computer Science club at @SCSU in New Haven for students In terms of my open source contribution I focus a lot on leadership development development and ensuring pathways of participation or wr","date":"2018-04-19","published":"2018-04-19T11:07:59+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/petermolnar/status/986873297995489280","tags":["openbadges"],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:71bcc506348b3819beefe21ce2d001cc","url":"/archive/known/?id=71bcc506348b3819beefe21ce2d001cc","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"Hey @GauthRaj how is my favorite #DigitalLiteracy guru. I hope things are well. #indieweb is a loose collective of technologists, bloggers, and activi","summary":"Hey @GauthRaj how is my favorite #DigitalLiteracy guru. I hope things are well. #indieweb is a loose collective of technologists, bloggers, and activist committed to owning your own data away from social media silos, controlling how and when you share this data with others, and crating tools that allow us to stay connected without relying on @twitter @facebo","date":"2018-04-19","published":"2018-04-19T11:02:30+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/GauthRaj/status/986854694264827904","tags":["DigitalLiteracy","indieweb"],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:064ea5b7ceac6158c94142e358fe50ac","url":"/archive/known/?id=064ea5b7ceac6158c94142e358fe50ac","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"@lonseidman I will never see gigabit service in East Haddam. Our last mile will never have fiber. It barely works now. I also find the lower upstream ","summary":"@lonseidman I will never see gigabit service in East Haddam. Our last mile will never have fiber. It barely works now. I also find the lower upstream to be a bit strange? I know the Tos probably doesn't allow runnign servers but they could bump that a bit. I think what CT needs to do is invest in municipal wifi. We have let the telcoms strangle us for too lo","date":"2018-04-18","published":"2018-04-18T19:03:59+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"http://www.ctnewsjunkie.com/archives/entry/20180417_comcast_adds_gigabit_downloads_faster_uploads_to_ct_customers/","tags":[],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
