{"id":"known:bcb1243ba4c7b829da3596a6200ed5ca","url":"/archive/known/?id=bcb1243ba4c7b829da3596a6200ed5ca","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"As a note just wanted to share I am more of a consumer of #indieweb tools rather than a producer. Been trying to apply the principles in my #highered ","summary":"As a note just wanted to share I am more of a consumer of #indieweb tools rather than a producer. Been trying to apply the principles in my #highered classes with a bunch of other #digped folks tracing lineage to #ds106 and #rhizo15 #rhizo16 Hopped back into the community. Funny what you find you have time for when you quit facebook.","date":"2018-04-12","published":"2018-04-12T15:10:44+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"http://quickthoughts.jgregorymcverry.com/2018/04/12/what-exactly-is-indieweb-and-how-can-we-talk-about","tags":["digped","ds106","highered","indieweb","rhizo15","rhizo16"],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:84c760968f6b6b6d49948c681b51020e","url":"/archive/known/?id=84c760968f6b6b6d49948c681b51020e","source":"known","type":"articles","title":"What exactly is #indieweb and how can we talk about it?","summary":"Across the numerous indieweb channels people have started to talk about how to discuss indieweb as the community and tools evolve into versions 2, 3, 4. Folks refer to these more as generations rather than traditional version conventions used in software development. The basic gist of the problem to me boiled down to mission, audience, and purpose. First and","date":"2018-04-12","published":"2018-04-12T13:56:43+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"tags":["IndieWeb","indieweb"],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:4273c643744480532ae2ac340940fc7a","url":"/archive/known/?id=4273c643744480532ae2ac340940fc7a","source":"known","type":"replies","title":"@mrkrndvs Most of my subdomains or for up MOOCs or pop-up learning events. I have found since so many users are new to Wordpress trying to do feeds fo","summary":"@mrkrndvs Most of my subdomains or for up MOOCs or pop-up learning events. I have found since so many users are new to Wordpress trying to do feeds for different catalogs, let alone post-kinds or other #indieweb tools to be difficult for them to follow. Plus I like pretty. Different communities deserve different stylesheets.","date":"2018-04-12","published":"2018-04-12T13:03:03+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/mrkrndvs/status/984404776212299777","tags":["indieweb"],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
