{"id":"known:ade0559b5c318c8c5717c3de822af3e7","url":"/archive/known/?id=ade0559b5c318c8c5717c3de822af3e7","source":"known","type":"articles","title":"Reflection on the #teachtheweb @MozTeach Curriculum Call","summary":"So we had a #teachtheweb call today (note using hashtag to encapsulate the combined curriculum and teach like @mozilla calls around a shred goal) Here is my brief feedback: We had a new moderator today. It was great to work with Robert Friedman from Hive Chicago. Hope we don't lose the snarky banter, or at least just save it for the chat window, but working ","date":"2015-06-02","published":"2015-06-02T22:26:41+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"tags":[],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:96bb515fcf12b89c3bb150fe2fcc20dd","url":"/archive/known/?id=96bb515fcf12b89c3bb150fe2fcc20dd","source":"known","type":"notes","title":"@MozTeach I would suggest in no particular order (as CSS gets complicated) Movie Poster, the Business Card, The About Me Page, and Make a Meme. We des","summary":"@MozTeach I would suggest in no particular order (as CSS gets complicated) Movie Poster, the Business Card, The About Me Page, and Make a Meme. We design a web literacy basics curriculum for Club Captains focused on recruiting. Then a \"Hello World\" activity for members. Just choose the Thimble Makes that cover the basics and fit the clubs well.","date":"2015-06-02","published":"2015-06-02T00:47:50+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/MozTeach/status/605522136615292928","tags":[],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
