{"id":"known:6ff5c24763293c2ec280a2fcc13077a7","url":"/archive/known/?id=6ff5c24763293c2ec280a2fcc13077a7","source":"known","type":"articles","title":"The Problem with List Servs and #ConnectedLearning","summary":"List servs work, and work well. That's there major drawback. It is hard to move academics off of a tool that has functioned long before the Web. Yes it comes with the baggage of bad email practices we suffer through at work: Unecessary reply-alls, threads being hijacked, threads getting too long and complex, people replying to older threads with totally new ","date":"2015-03-25","published":"2015-03-25T01:36:29+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"tags":[],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:df31a5835b870ef2f0aee8378d74f9c3","url":"/archive/known/?id=df31a5835b870ef2f0aee8378d74f9c3","source":"known","type":"photos","title":"Thinking #teachtheweb long game","summary":"Had a great club call today. Debated on whether to meet in April. This was the last call of the quarter. I guess that is the private sector equivalent of the end of the semester. I think people are tired. Rightfully so. As soon as the Web Literacy Map and the Club Curriculum teams finished everyone had to hit the hyperdrive. Content was written by the #teach","date":"2015-03-25","published":"2015-03-25T01:04:57+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"tags":[],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
