{"id":"known:c6ba2b1f2bcb8412cb02aeeb0ffc8a07","url":"/archive/known/?id=c6ba2b1f2bcb8412cb02aeeb0ffc8a07","source":"known","type":"articles","title":"Quick Thoughts on the #teachtheweb \"Club Call\"","summary":"I enjoy the club calls as much as the web literacy calls. Whereas the web lit calls invogorate my mind the club calls spark my passion for teaching. Today was no different. We had a lot of fun taking stock of where the curriculum has come. The Mozilla Learning team does fantastic work at a tough pace. It helps when you draw on the experience of MOUSE and oth","date":"2015-03-11","published":"2015-03-11T01:22:40+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"tags":[],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
{"id":"known:a75ec403b340850ade4ab62cb8205a7b","url":"/archive/known/?id=a75ec403b340850ade4ab62cb8205a7b","source":"known","type":"articles","title":"Quick Thoughts to the Webmaker Club Roll Out Plan","summary":"These are just quick unorganized thoughts as my reaction to the webmaker club roll out plan If you asked the next billion web users who come online do you want them to say, \"I am a webmaker\" or \"I am a Mozillian?\" Both goals are fine, both are united by the same values, but the latter pushes a brand before learning. If that is the goal then the new name Mozi","date":"2015-03-10","published":"2015-03-10T14:30:08+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"tags":[],"access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published"}
